@rick1082 I was actually of the impression that one could not detects loss of a CIS connection, but only the ACL by use of the link supervision timeout. Have I missed something here?
I think the intension in BLE Audio is that the audio source shall keep transmitting the CIS data as long as the ACL is connected - this allows audio data to flow even in the cases where the ACK packets are lost - which can happen when there is a significant difference in TX power of the audio source and audio sink devices - the typical case for a phone and a TWIE device. It would allow the ACL to use for example 1mbit or coded phy while the CIS uses 1 or 2MBit.
But I do agree in the ACL dropped case, but also the connect to device 1 first, and then when device 2 is found you attach that as well. This will allow for 1) the user might only have power on one of the TWIE devices even though there are two in the set. 2) the connection/stream to device 1 can be setup immediately when it is found, potentially speeding up the total connection time.

